--TEST--
reading a file that is not there under a granted folder throws an `IOError` whose second line says that a relative path in the source starts at the folder of its file — `rule:programs/path-literals-resolve-from-their-file`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// The literal is joined to the folder of this file, and no file is there.
try {
    echo Core\IO::read('data/missing.txt');
} catch (IOError $error) {
    echo Core\Str::after($error->message, "\n"), "\n";
}
--FILE data/note.txt--
read
--FILE nvs.toml--
[capabilities.fs]
read = ["./data"]
--EXPECT--
help: a relative path written in the source starts at the folder of the file that contains it
